# Blend modes on paper, 256x64. Six cells left to right; each is a gold (232,179,58) 36x36 square with a blue
# (79,127,224) circle of radius 13 centered 10px right of the square's center, so the circle covers the square's right
# half and spills past its right edge. The circle carries a blend: key. `layer cells` is isolated, so the blend sees
# only the layer's own pixels: the part of the circle past the square's right edge has nothing under it and stays plain
# blue (79,127,224) in cells 2-5, same as cell 1. Only the overlap with the square changes.
# Cell 1: no blend, a plain blue circle. Cell 2: multiply, the overlap is a dark olive green, darker than both gold and
# blue. Cell 3: screen, the overlap is pale pink, lighter than both. Cell 4: overlay, the overlap is a muted tan-gold,
# distinct from plain blue. Cell 5: add, the overlap is plain white. Cell 6: erase, the circle cuts a round hole through
# the square and shows paper through it; the spill past the square's right edge erases nothing, so no blue shows there.
@artboard 256x64
@target shapes/blends.png

layer cells
  rect 36x36 at:21,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:31,32 fill:p.blue
  rect 36x36 at:63,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:73,32 fill:p.blue blend:multiply
  rect 36x36 at:105,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:115,32 fill:p.blue blend:screen
  rect 36x36 at:147,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:157,32 fill:p.blue blend:overlay
  rect 36x36 at:189,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:199,32 fill:p.blue blend:add
  rect 36x36 at:231,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:241,32 fill:p.blue blend:erase
